    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nTracks \"Phase 2\" items from https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/34281 , specifically: \n\n- some users may enjoy entering the pager every time a big message is displayed\n- graduate height settings to a real option such as `'messagesheight'`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n- [ ] Let the 'more' option control whether the pager is focused? (This will slightly change the purpose of the option.) \"Off\" by default.\n    - Or the existing `messagesopt=hit-enter` flag?\n- [x] Introduce a ~~'messagesheight'~~ `'messagesopt':\"maxheight\"` option, instead of `'cmdheight'`. This controls the maximum height of text shown by default. The pager is still never focused by default, but output is shown up to 'messagesheight' and may overlay the current buffer. \n    - https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41474\n    - The user cursor position remains in whatever buffer they were in when they invoked a mapping/command that triggered output. \n    - The pager disappears on any kind of user input. It is not timer-based.\n    - As always, if 'messagesheight' didn't show enough, the user hits `g<` to opt-in to the full pager.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
