            "body": "> did you try set `messagesopt+=maxheight:50`?\n\nI did; that's actually the default (according to the docs anyway). Either way, it doesn't work:\n\n- `:lua require('vim._core.ui2').enable()`\n- `:set messagesopt+=maxheight:50`\n- `:hi`\n  <img width=\"865\" height=\"561\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78591abb-d7ec-48ac-b25e-40a6f1043d99\" />\n- `g<`\n  <img width=\"865\" height=\"561\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5b6b9abc-b0a0-45a1-8e7c-04d1b7594d85\" />\n\n> are we pretty sure we won't need other dimenions? like width/border?\n\nI wouldn't use them but I could imagine others would be interested in them. More customization is good.",
